ent-ShiptestMobGoliathWhitesands = goliath
    .desc = A species of goliath native to sand planets. While its shell can take more punishment, it also has much weaker skin to compensate.
ent-ShiptestMobGoliathWhitesandsAncient = ancient goliath
    .desc = Goliaths are biologically immortal, and rare specimens have survived for centuries. This one is clearly ancient, and its shell is dangerously durable.
ent-ShiptestMobGruboid = gruboid
    .desc = What appears to be a tremendous burrowing worm. Its burrowing tendrils ensnare prey, leaving them helpless.
ent-ShiptestMobGruboidBaby = baby gruboid
    .desc = A newly-born gruboid. Though its hide is less durable than that of a mature gruboid, it is equally capable of defending itself.
ent-ShiptestMobBasiliskWhitesands = basilisk
    .desc = A native beast of sand planets. This unique mutation has evolved a shell around its body, deflecting all attacks until broken.
ent-ShiptestMobLavagrub = lavagrub
    .desc = A worm that grows fat from eating everything in its sight. This mutation, seen on lava planetoids, sets things on fire. Probably to ward off predators.
ent-ShiptestEffectTurfFire = fire
ent-ShiptestGoliathTentacleSnare = tentacle mass
ent-ShiptestMobGoliathCrystal = crystal goliath
    .desc = Once a goliath, now an abominable mass of twisted flesh and crystals that sprout throughout its decomposing body.
ent-ShiptestMobLegionCrystal = disfigured legion
    .desc = Disfigured, contorted, and corrupted. This thing was once part of the legion, now it has a different vile and twisted allegiance.
ent-ShiptestMobLegionCrystalHead = disfigured legion
    .desc = One of none.
ent-ShiptestMobWatcherForgotten = forgotten watcher
    .desc = This watcher has a cancerous crystal growth on it, forever scarring it and deforming it into this twisted form.
ent-ShiptestBoltBasiliskSuper = freezing blast
ent-ShiptestProjectileCrystalShard = crystalline shard
ent-ShiptestEffectCrystalSpire = crystalline spire
ent-ShiptestCrystalSpire = crystalline spire
ent-ShiptestEffectCrystalSpireRetract = crystalline spire
ent-ShiptestMobWolf = white wolf
    .desc = A beast that survives by feasting on weaker opponents. They're much stronger with numbers. Watch out for the lunge!
ent-ShiptestMobWolfAlpha = alpha wolf
    .desc = An old wolf with matted, dirty fur and a missing eye, trophies of many won battles and successful hunts. Seems like it's the leader of the pack around here. Watch out for the lunge!
ent-ShiptestMobLobstrosityArctic = arctic lobstrosity
    .desc = A marvel of evolution gone wrong. The frosty ice produces underground lakes where these ill-tempered seafood gather. Beware its charge.
ent-ShiptestMobLobstrosityTropical = tropical lobstrosity
    .desc = A marvel of evolution gone wrong. On the tropical beaches, its diet of crabs gives it a red-hued shell. Beware its charge.
ent-ShiptestMobIceWhelp = ice whelp
    .desc = The offspring of an ice drake, weak in comparison but still terrifying.
ent-ShiptestMobIceDemon = demonic watcher
    .desc = A creature formed entirely out of ice. Bluespace energy emanates from inside of it.
ent-ShiptestMobIceDemonPrimordial = primordial demon
    .desc = At the beginning, there was nothing but emptiness. From the emptiness, there came monsters.
ent-ShiptestBoltIce = ice blast
ent-ShiptestEffectFireBreath = fire breath
ent-ShiptestMobBrimdemon = brimdemon
    .desc = A misshapen demon with big, red eyes and a hinged mouth. Not much is known about the creatures, because they answer anything unexpected with a "brimbeam", a deadly blood-laser barrage.
ent-ShiptestEffectBrimbeamWarning = brimbeam
ent-ShiptestBrimbeam = brimbeam
ent-ShiptestMobAntlion = antlion
    .desc = A large insectoid creature.
ent-ShiptestMobAntlionQueen = antlion queen
    .desc = A huge antlion. It looks displeased.
ent-ShiptestAntlionBurrow = burrow
ent-ShiptestEffectSandSplash = sand
ent-ShiptestMobBearBrown = brown bear
    .desc = A ferocious brown bear, ready to maul.
ent-ShiptestMobBearPolar = polar bear
    .desc = An aggressive animal that defends its territory with incredible power. These beasts don't run from their enemies.
ent-ShiptestMobBearWar = polar warbear
    .desc = An aggressive animal that defends its territory with incredible power. This one appears to be a remnant of the short-lived Wojtek-Aleph program.
ent-ShiptestMobLegate = legate
    .desc = A rare and incredibly dangerous legion mutation, formed from a plethora of legions joined in union around a young necropolis spire. It's looking particularly self-confident.
ent-ShiptestMobSeedling = seedling
    .desc = This oversized, predatory flower conceals what can only be described as an organic energy cannon.
ent-ShiptestProjectileSolar = solar energy

