ent-ShiptestMaterialSinew = watcher sinew
    .desc = Long stringy filaments which presumably came from a watcher's wings.
ent-ShiptestMaterialSinewWolf = wolf sinew
    .desc = Long stringy filaments which came from the insides of a wolf.
ent-ShiptestMaterialHideAshDrake = ash drake hide
    .desc = The strong, scaled hide of an ash drake.
ent-ShiptestBrimdust = brimdust
    .desc = Dust from a brimdemon. It is considered valuable for botanical and heating purposes.
ent-ShiptestStrangeCrystal = strange crystal
    .desc = A crystal that came from a dead creature. Its rapid growth and corruption is kept inert.
ent-ShiptestRegenerativeCoreLegion = regenerative core
    .desc = A strange rock that crackles with power. It can be used to heal completely, but it will rapidly decay into uselessness.
ent-ShiptestRegenerativeCoreCrystal = crystal heart
    .desc = A strange rock in the shape of a heart symbol. Applying will repair your body with crystals, but may have additional side effects. It seems it can't survive for very long outside a host.
ent-ShiptestBearArmor = pile of bear armor
    .desc = A scattered pile of various shaped armor pieces fitted for a bear, some duct tape, and a nail filer. Crude instructions are written on the back of one of the plates in russian. This seems like an awful idea.
ent-ShiptestHierophantClub = hierophant club
    .desc = The strange technology of this large club allows various nigh-magical feats. It used to beat you, but now you can set the beat.
ent-ShiptestGemBase = gem
ent-ShiptestGemRupee = Ruperium Crystal
    .desc = An exotic crystalline compound rarely found all over the frontier of known space. Has few practical uses, but the resonating properties it possesses make it highly valued in the creation of designer instruments.
ent-ShiptestGemFrostDiamond = Frost Diamond
    .desc = A rare form of crystalline carbon, most commonly found in the inner stone of crashed comets. Though asteroid mining long devalued more common forms of diamond, this one remains exclusive.
ent-ShiptestGemVoid = Null Crystal
    .desc = A shard of stellar energy, shaped into crystal. These strange objects occasionally appear spontaneously in the deepest, darkest depths of space. Despite it's incredible value, it seems far lighter than it should be.
ent-ShiptestGemPhoron = Stabilized Phoron
    .desc = When under incredible pressure during formation, plasma crystal is occasionally known to transform into this substance. Famed both for exceptional durability and uncommon beauty.
ent-ShiptestGemAmber = Draconic Amber
    .desc = The final decompositional result of a dragon's white-hot blood. Cherished by inner-world gemcutters for its soft warmth and faint glow.
ent-ShiptestTrophyBase = tail spike
    .desc = A strange spike with no usage.
ent-ShiptestTrophyGoliathTentacle = goliath tentacle
    .desc = A sliced-off goliath tentacle.
ent-ShiptestTrophyElderTentacle = elder tentacle
    .desc = The barbed tip of a tentacle sliced from an incredibly ancient goliath.
ent-ShiptestTrophyWatcherWing = watcher wing
    .desc = A wing ripped from a watcher.
ent-ShiptestTrophyWolfEar = wolf ear
    .desc = The battered remains of a wolf's ear. You could attach it to a crusher, or use the fur to craft a trophy.
ent-ShiptestTrophyFang = battle-stained fang
    .desc = A wolf fang, displaying the wear and tear associated with a long and colorful life. Could be attached to a kinetic crusher or used to make a trophy.
ent-ShiptestTrophyLobsterClaw = lobster claw
    .desc = A lobster claw.
ent-ShiptestTrophyBrimdemonFang = brimdemon's fang
    .desc = A fang from a brimdemon's corpse.
ent-ShiptestTrophyVortexTalisman = vortex talisman
    .desc = A glowing trinket that was originally the Hierophant's beacon.
ent-ShiptestTrophyTailSpike = tail spike
    .desc = A spike taken from a young dragon's tail. Sharp enough to stab someone with.
ent-ShiptestFuguGland = wumborian fugu gland
    .desc = The key to the wumborian fugu's ability to increase its mass arbitrarily, this disgusting remnant can apply the same effect to other creatures, giving them great strength.
